=== note on the two lanes ===
Zero SKIP lines in either lane (`grep -c '^SKIP' = 0` in both): every one of
the 80 assertions genuinely executed on this platform. The two lanes assert
the SAME 80 things - sorting each lane's assertion text and diffing leaves
exactly ONE line on each side, and it is the mirror-image self-registration
check (the POSIX lane asserts ...tests.ps1 twin exists, the PowerShell lane
asserts ...tests.sh twin exists). The remaining 18 raw-diff lines are pure
ORDERING: the six handshake assertions (handshake-block-present and
handshake-tokens for PLUGIN-CONTRACTS.md, bootstrap and the interviewer) are
emitted at a different point in each runtime's per-document loop. No
assertion is present in one lane and absent in the other, so unlike T-010
this task's two lanes tally IDENTICALLY at 80 rather than differing.

Composition of the 80, decomposed from the section markers rather than taken
on trust (counted in the POSIX lane; the PowerShell lane matches):
  21  live document conformance (TEST-024 / TEST-035P / TEST-039)
   6  fixture construction (TEST-026 / TEST-039)
   9  six independent present-but-invalid reasons (TEST-026)
  24  six-case matrix x four documents (TEST-039)
   4  the two routes are genuinely distinct (TEST-026)
  13  mutation detection power (TEST-MUT)
   3  self-registration
  --
  80

The two lanes are genuinely independent readers of the same four documents,
not one reader run twice: the POSIX lane extracts the delimited six-case
table with an embedded python3 program (tests/plugin-contracts-track-
selection.tests.sh:73-78 resolves the interpreter, :216 skips the alignment
row), while the PowerShell lane parses it with its own native cmdlet code
(tests/plugin-contracts-track-selection.tests.ps1:125 Get-ContractRows, :138
alignment-row skip, :352 Get-DocResolution). python3 appears in the
PowerShell lane only as the fixture/signer/validator driver (:40), never as
the table extractor, and neither suite invokes the other.

The 24 six-case routing assertions are 6 cases x 4 documents
(PLUGIN-CONTRACTS.md, bootstrap/SKILL.md, sdd-bootstrap-interviewer/SKILL.md,
lite-gate/SKILL.md). The two PROTECTED consumers (ship/SKILL.md,
lite-spec/SKILL.md) are deliberately absent from this matrix - they are
T-012's scope, and AC-039's full five-consumer matrix therefore remains
T-012-owned. Both lanes complete in seconds; no long-running lane here.
